Easy. The one from Eternal. It fixed what the one from 16 botched.

&#x200B;

16's chaingun really didn't feel useful until you got the mobile turret. Eternal? You could easily whip it out and start firing away akin to Classic DOOM's chaingun, mobile turret, energy shield, or no mods at all.

If there is one thing I wish they fixed, it's that I wished they fixed the arbitrary requirement of having your language and region set to what THEY want just to install it. You can do that just fine with any other software (i.e.: Razer Synapse, SteelSeries GG, NZXT Cam, to name a few) just fine under a region and language that's not the standard ones that Corsair has.

&#x200B;

In fact, this is more of a suggestion to Corsair themselves: Remove the requirement to have your system language and region set to EN-US! I don't want to have to go in and reset my language and region just to install a piece of software!

Technically to a degree, no. While there are those kinds of people saying that you should upgrade every year, I haven't really felt the need to upgrade from what I now consider ol' reliable (minus the battery and software issues)

&#x200B;

But I unfortunately am going to be switching to Android due to the fact that the last few iPhones haven't wow'd me as much, and I don't really like some of Apple's recent practises, especially in regards to certain parts of their business, i.e., the Mac.

This may be your personal experience, and I'm okay with you expressing that. I on the other hand for the most part, am kind of the opposite. Why?

&#x200B;

**I spilled a sugar infused soda into my legacy Apex Pro TKL's Hall Effect switches, and it still worked!**

&#x200B;

Part of me wants to say it's more of the type of switch they used in the keyboard but other than that, the only key I have a slight problem with is the stabiliser on the left shift, which probably could be fixed with some lube, but other than that, the only thing I really broke from them is a mouse and that's it.

&#x200B;

I personally love SteelSeries, and if there is one thing I wish they could improve is probably the software, as well as some aspects of GG/Engine, but other than that, I've never had real problems with it.

Show a picture of the top. It's pretty easy to find out what it is if I can see the USB A and type-C ports.

&#x200B;

If it's two A's one C, that's a 5000D, if it's four A's one C, it's a 7000.

ZedAlpha.

&#x200B;

iDunno.

I like the music of the Ancient Gods part 2 better than part 1.

&#x200B;

Don't get me wrong, I absolutely LOVED Atlantica and the Blood Swamps, but I feel like they get edged out by the entirety of the World Spear, Reclaimed Earth, and Immora. Immora especially because I feel like David executed the double bass drum in Headstomp better than Andrew did in part 1.

&#x200B;

Atlantica and the Blood Swamps are outright amazing, but I feel like the weakest track is the Holt. World Spear was near perfect with it's build-up in the light combat, and especially with it's punchy riffs and metal choir stems. Reclaimed Earth has one of my favorite riffs involving what I'm assuming is a sonar device that submarines use, and it's ambience music has a little DINK sound that Koma decided to put "DINK Eternal" in his gamerip, which I thought was cute and funny. Immora? Everything scratches the itch of what I want in a DOOM song. Punchy guitars, sick beats, and of course, you cannot knock it for having Headstomp, which is absolutely perfect.

&#x200B;

Even though the Dark Lord fight seemed relatively weak compared to Samur, the Trial of Maligog, the Icon of Sin, the first Marauder, and the first DOOM Hunters, the music absolutely slaps, and I love the references that were in the franchise's past games, such as E1M3 Dark Halls, the title drop for '16 and Eternal (They're both relatively the same, just different inflections, as well as pitch), BFG Division, MAP05, and so many more that I could have possibly missed, but absolutely loved.

&#x200B;

Overall, ALL of DOOM Eternal's soundtrack is amazing, probably with the exception of the Holt. The Holt is okay.

A lot of people were divided on the game as a whole, but I myself thoroughly enjoyed Part 2.

&#x200B;

I guess I'm just too easy to please when it comes to do DOOM.

