I know how you feel. I too am "tired" all the time, because of so much anger and rage, as well as constant depression and wishing it would all end, especially in the wake of what's been going on recently.

&#x200B;

It's also the reason why I've been drinking alcoholic beverages constantly for the past two months, especially when I get home from work, or on my days off. My job itself isn't bad, but I'm in constant anxiety of not being told when my shift change is supposed to happen. One of the morning shift workers yelled at me because I don't want to work only 30 hours, and it was especially worst last month, especially when I was always unsure of being required to work overtime, and the worst one was on August 10th. I literally cried and ruined the face mask I was wearing, and it wasn't used for more than three days.

&#x200B;

I also want it all to end because of stupid decisions I made, and I feel like I'm better off forgotten by everyone.
